    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this is the fare on trip TRP-00114 (Bugis Junction to Jurong East, Friday 7 August 2026), charged at SGD 58.10. The rider accepts the 1.6 surge and disputes only the extra distance. Both advocates agree on the core facts, and so do I.\n\nRoute deviation. All three platform artifacts carry trip_id TRP-00114 and the trace's first fix (18:40) matches the recorded start, so the trip is identified and the rider's limb (a) under POL-RD-08 is met. On distance the GPS polyline governs: EV-GPS-00114 records 23.97 km, and that is the figure I use, not the rounded 24.0 km on the trip record. Against the booked optimal of 18.0 km (EV-TRIP-00114) the excess is 5.97 km, or 33.17%. That clears both POL-RD-01 gates (above 20% and above 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and limb (b) is met. It does not reach materiality (which needs more than 50% or more than 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile review, FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral arises.\n\nTrace integrity. 241 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, with no 500 m jumps. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.\n\nExoneration. Nothing excuses the deviation. No endpoint was amended (the POL-RD-05 fields are null). The chat log shows the rider challenging the route and the driver answering that he chose the corridor; there is no rider instruction and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable. The driver's explanation — that the AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit — is a traffic ground, and to exonerate under POL-RD-03 it needs a traffic advisory naming the affected segment with an overlapping validity window. EV-ADVIS-00114-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no LTA advisory covers the AYE, PIE or Alexandra corridor in the 18:36-19:20 window. Under POL-GEN-02 that absence is citable but carries no fact and does not cap my confidence, because the facts that decide this case sit on the clean, weight-1.0 artifacts. I have considered whether the absent advisory should send the case to a human reviewer. It should not: POL-RD-08 provides that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver's burden, and POL-RD-10(5) has nothing to bite on because the driver named no advisory to be missing. The record is complete and sufficient to rule.\n\nFare arithmetic (metered, so POL-RD-02 applies):\n- charged_total: SGD 58.10\n- recomputed_fare: (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.0 + 0.28 x 30.0) x 1.6 + 0.80 + 2.50 = 25.70 x 1.6 + 3.30 = 41.12 + 3.30 = SGD 44.42\n- refund: 58.10 - 44.42 = SGD 13.68, rounded up to SGD 13.70.\nThe surge multiplier of 1.6 is read from EV-FARE-00114 and the rider accepts it. The recomputed fare credits only the ERP on the optimal route, the Kim Keat Link gantry at 2.50. The Adam Road gantry at 2.00 is off the optimal route and is already comprehended in the refund under POL-RD-09(1); it is not added on top. Both billed gantries sit within 250 m of trace fixes (0.0 m and 8.8 m), so neither is a phantom line and there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding.\n\nNo driver compensation is due: the distance billed (24.0 km) is not less than the trace records, so the POL-RD-04 compensation limb does not arise. The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and below 90% of the total, so this is a partial, not a full, refund.\n\nOutcome: SGD 13.70 is returned to the rider; the remainder of the fare stands."
