    "explanation": "To both parties — ruling on trip TRP-00114 (Bugis Junction to Jurong East MRT, Friday 7 August 2026).\n\nDEVIATION. The governing distance is the GPS trace, not the trip record's rounded copy: POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km (23.97 km) govern over the 24.0 km convenience figure, against a booked optimal of 18.0 km. The excess is 5.97 km, or 33.2% of optimal, clearing both the 0.8 km and 20% establishment gates, so the deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (241 fixes, 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, zero gaps), so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The excess does NOT reach MATERIALITY (which needs above 50% or above 8.0 km), so no driver-profile pattern finding arises and no conduct referral follows. The driver's own trailing-90-day figures (deviation_flags_90d 1 over 412 completed trips) would not establish a pattern in any event; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used.\n\nFARE. The trip is METERED, so the remedy is the arithmetic of POL-RD-02, carrying the 1.6 surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier — which the rider accepts.\n  • Charged_total: 58.10\n  • Recomputed_fare: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 18.0 + 0.28 x 30) x 1.6) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 on-route ERP = (25.70 x 1.6) + 3.30 = 44.42\n  • Refund: 58.10 - 44.42 = 13.68, rounded up to SGD 13.70\nThe 2.00 Adam Road gantry is off the optimal route but is already comprehended in that 13.70 — the recomputed fare credits only the on-route Kim Keat Link gantry — so it is itemised for transparency and is NOT added on top (POL-RD-09(1)). Both billed gantries are matched crossings (the trace passes within 250 m of each), so no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) is available. The refund is above the 0.50 de minimis and below 90% of the charge, so it is a PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\nEXCULPATION. POL-RD-03 cannot run: it